@*
    What each of the empire's choices does, one option at a time.

    The panel it sits in adds everything up; this takes it apart again. The totals answer "what is my
    empire like", and this answers "which of my choices did that" - the question you have when a
    number is not what you expected, and which was previously answerable only by hovering each row of
    the totals to read its tooltip.

    Everything an option does, not only its numbers. Most of what an option does is not a number:
    Aerospace Adaptation's three modifiers say nothing about the biological ships it is actually
    about, and forty-two of the game's seventy-seven origins carry no modifier at all - which is why
    Prosperous Unification used to be missing from this list entirely.

    Rendered by the same component the hover popover uses, so an option cannot say one thing there
    and another here. The lore paragraph is not part of it: that belongs to the chip, above the
    effects, and a column of flavour text is not what this panel is for.
*@

@if (Contributions.Count == 0)
{
    <p class="sem-hint">Nothing chosen so far changes anything.</p>
}

@foreach (var contribution in Contributions)
{
    <div class="option" @key="contribution.Option.Key">
        <div class="name">
            <GameIcon Path="@contribution.Option.Icon" Alt="" />
            <span>@contribution.Option.Name</span>
        </div>

        @*
            AllModifiers, because this has to add up to the total above it. An option may ask for its
            numbers not to be listed - its own sentence usually states them - and the arithmetic
            counts them regardless, so a breakdown that honoured the request would not reconcile.
        *@
        <EffectsList Effects="@contribution.Effects" AllModifiers="true" />
    </div>
}

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Each option that changes something, with what it changes.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required IReadOnlyList<OptionContribution> Contributions { get; set; }
}
